From 80a467f105358abd03b227b1886107e153ad2daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:16:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] qwen4exp: copy the conv-state tail straight into each
 rollback slot

For every linear-attention layer and every rollback slot the graph copied the
strided conv-state tail into a contiguous temporary and then into the slot:
two copy kernels where one does (ggml_cpy accepts the strided view; on CUDA it
becomes one 2D memcpy).  With MTP n-max 3 that is ~4 slots x 36 layers = ~144
kernels per verify graph removed, each costing the ~3 us dependent-dispatch
gap that dominates decode.  LLAMA_CONV_TAIL_CONT=1 restores the old graph for
A/B.

2 x R9700, qwen4exp + MTP (n-max 3, p-min 0), -sm tensor -ub 2048, greedy
300-token requests, warm: 110.8-111.9 -> 113.6-114.4 t/s on one prompt,
100.4-102.3 -> 102.9-104.4 on another; greedy output unchanged;
GGML_META_SS_VERIFY=1 clean; KL divergence vs the old graph (wikitext 16 x
2048): 0.000000 mean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/models/qwen4exp.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
index 2ff812462..ef9159969 100644
--- a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
@@ -2845,7 +2845,10 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_conv_state_at(
                 conv_states_all->nb[1],
                 (slot * mem_size + kv_head) * row_size);
 
-        ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, ggml_cpy(ctx0, ggml_cont(ctx0, tail), dst));
+        // copy the strided tail straight into the slot (one copy, a 2D memcpy on CUDA) instead of cont + cpy;
+        // LLAMA_CONV_TAIL_CONT=1 restores the intermediate contiguous copy for A/B
+        static const bool tail_cont = getenv("LLAMA_CONV_TAIL_CONT") != nullptr && atoi(getenv("LLAMA_CONV_TAIL_CONT")) != 0;
+        ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, ggml_cpy(ctx0, tail_cont ? ggml_cont(ctx0, tail) : tail, dst));
     }
 
     return conv_input;
